  </div><a href="https://github.com/AutoByteus/autobyteus-nfs/blob/v0.1.0/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="mt-3 inline-block text-sm font-semibold text-blue-700 underline underline-offset-4">Public CLI documentation and advanced flags (v0.1.0)</a>
  <p class="mt-5 rounded-xl border border-blue-100 bg-blue-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-blue-900">Use the printed mount path as an ordinary directory. AutoByteus does not check its mount type or storage identity. For the Docker launcher, choose an operator-managed shared root with shared/ and nodes/&lt;name&gt;/ subdirectories.</p>
  <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-amber-950">
    <p class="font-semibold">Use only on a trusted private network</p>
    <p class="mt-1">NFS traffic is unencrypted. Access trusts the allowed computers, not individual users; writes map to the selected nonroot source owner. Connection details are not an access token. Do not expose this service to the public internet.</p>
    <p class="mt-2">If storage or the network goes offline, file operations, previews and unrelated work may stall. Restore connectivity before retrying; there is no offline copy or local fallback.</p>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">Mac Docker storage hosting and Windows are not supported. The service does not attach or restart application containers. The Docker Guide configures ordinary directory binds separately.</p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-slate-500">Downloads are available; physical-host, shared-filesystem, independent-client and user testing remains deferred. Availability does not prove host readiness. Checksums do not replace publisher trust, signing or operating-system security checks.</p>
</section>
